rewritten-to-match
Same algorithm: build the tree from the stored frequencies, walk it bit by bit over the packed bytes. The tree's Box nodes are arrays. The reference allocates a zeroed output of bit_count bytes (about 2.7 MB) each run and truncates it; here the output is a state array of the input's size that is only written as far as the decoded text, so the reference also pays for the allocation (lazily zeroed pages) that this does not. The encoder that prepares the input is untimed, as in the reference; the equality test with the input runs in the checksum request. Stores are checked and undo-logged.
